++
++    fix(absorb): wire existing runbook into absorb_proposal for update action. Addresses LORE-069.
++    
++    LORE-069: absorb_proposal called propose(class_id) with no `existing`
++    argument, so EVERY absorb payload said "action": "new" with `added`
++    byte-identical to the runbook the class already has — the diff engine
++    (compiler.py) was exercised only by tests, and PRD US-2's "drafts the
++    runbook update ... evidence blocks, dead ends marked dead" was unmet.
++    
++    Both halves of the row's locus are fixed:
++    
++    1. The call: absorb_proposal (lore/absorb.py) now compiles the class's
++       existing runbook and calls propose(class_id, existing=..., fresh=...)
++       — the greppable AC (grep -rn 'existing=' lore/*.py) has its
++       production hit at lore/absorb.py:315. Signature unchanged for CLI
++       compatibility: (class_id, lesson, source=None); a keyword-only
++       `blocks` parameter was added (callers may hand already-parsed
++       evidence entries; absorb_sweep passes its classified blocks through
++       with kind/observed_at/source intact — absorb_sweep's signature is
++       untouched).
++    
++    2. The content: propose's fresh side becomes a runbook with the trail
++       evidence FOLDED in — without this, registry-vs-registry diffing is
++       empty by construction and "update" would claim a delta that contains
++       nothing (the row's explicit warning about label-only fixes). Folding
++       reuses the existing machinery: evidence entries -> attach_evidence
++       appends them to evidence_trail (append-only, so removed stays {});
++       lesson prose is parsed per-line with parse_text_line — now a public
++       seam over the sweep's internal parser, so the exact --window
++       tolerance is shared, not re-implemented. propose gained an additive
++       keyword-only `fresh` parameter (default compile_class(class_id)
++       unchanged); existing callers and tests are untouched.
++    
++    US-2 rendering: every folded block also lands in the payload's `blocks`
++    list as {kind, detail, source, observed_at, outcome}, `outcome` being a
++    closed vocabulary "dead-end"/"observed" (block_outcome; word-bounded
++    dead-end markers so "deadline"/"undead" never trigger). A trail that
++    adds nothing yields an explicitly EMPTY update (action still "update",
++    added/changed/removed all {} — never the fabricated "new").
++    
++    Propose-not-write holds: nothing is written anywhere; verified by the
++    existing no-filesystem-writes guards, still green.
++    
++    Tests: 13 new at the absorb_proposal seam (update case with
++    trail-derived added.evidence_trail; no-change trail and prose-only
++    lesson both explicitly-empty updates; closed outcome vocabulary;
++    word-boundary markers; unclassified absorption; unknown-class fail-safe;
++    parser-tolerance reuse; propose fresh-side default equivalence; sweep
++    and CLI paths emitting update). Stale pin flipped: the lone --class
++    path was pinned to action == "new" (the defect itself). Count sync:
++    544 -> 557 (scripts/test-count.txt, README, INSTALL, CONTRIBUTING,
++    skills/lore-usage) — count guard PASS.
++    
++    Docs reconciled: README sweep paragraph and CHANGELOG entry describe
++    the real update action; skills/lore-usage SKILL.md's run-14c section
++    ("absorb never proposes an UPDATE — do not read action as truth")
++    rewritten to describe the fixed surface and name the residual limit
++    (the delta covers evidence_trail only).
++    
++    Gates: 557 passed; ruff check + format clean; count guard PASS; live
++    red/green probe at HEAD vs working tree: pre-fix action=new/no-blocks,
++    post-fix action=update with the lesson's evidence in added.evidence_trail.
